('shared_kernel/residual_drop.py',98,'Three-component residual-drop record accepts int/float including NaN/infinity; create/from_dict coerce first and can turn bool/string inputs into floats despite the direct constructor bool guard. Strict contraction means nonnegative components with positive sum, so positive infinity passes and no before/after binding is checked. This is approximate measurement metadata, not zero-float exact arithmetic.'),
('shared_kernel/disposition.py',90,'Disposition strips/uppercases arbitrary strings but never requires enum membership, so empty or unknown statuses are representable and merely nonterminal. Convenience factories yield known labels; none validates actual gate execution or acceptance evidence.'),
